Consider the recursive function:

def countCalls(n):
    if n <= 1:
        return 1
    return countCalls(n - 1) + countCalls(n - 2)

How many total invocations (calls) of `countCalls` are made to evaluate `countCalls(4)` (including the initial call)?

What integer value is returned by the function call `calc(3, 4)`?

def calc(base, exp):
    if exp == 0:
        return 1
    return base * calc(base, exp - 1)
